    "collapsible_content_FD4LGE": {
      "type": "collapsible-content",
      "blocks": {
        "collapsible_row_BRzHaB": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How does MoonShade RV attach to my trailer?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade RV has an integrated 3/8\" keder welt sewn into the canopy. It slides directly into your trailer's existing awning rail — no anchor hardware, no surface prep.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_Yr48NB": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What trailers is MoonShade RV compatible with?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade RV is built for lightweight towable trailers and pop-ups (generally under 20ft) with a standard 3/8\" keder or awning rail. Customer-confirmed trailers include the nuCamp T@B 320 and Forest River pop-ups. Most lightweight towables from Winnebago, Thor, Coachmen, Forest River, Jayco, and Fleetwood with a compatible rail will work. See the <a href=\"/pages/vehicle-compatibility-list\" title=\"Vehicle Compatibility List\">full list </a>here.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_gpLq9j": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Does MoonShade RV work on the Airstream Basecamp?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>No — the Basecamp uses a 1/2\" rail, not the standard 3/8\". Basecamp owners should use MoonShade (OG) with the dedicated Basecamp Awning Rail Anchor.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_tTRmj4": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Can I use MoonShade RV on a full-size motorhome or van?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>MoonShade RV is built for lightweight towables with keder rails. For full-size vans or motorhomes, MoonShade XL or MoonShade Pro is the better fit.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_nHrc4F": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MoonShade RV a good replacement for my factory awning?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>Yes — that's the most common reason customers buy it. It's lighter than most factory replacements, sets up and comes down faster, and packs into a bag when not in use.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        },
        "collapsible_row_cHfdCB": {
          "type": "collapsible_row",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Is MoonShade waterproof?",
            "icon": "none",
            "row_content": "<p>We don’t “waterproof” our fabric because it would degrade the integrity of its UV resistance over time. That said, it is seam-sealed and the fabric is a technical 420 ripstop that sheds water like an umbrella.</p>",
            "page": ""
          }
        }
      },
